WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:11.380
Mice that lack TRPM8, the cold and menthol receptor, were trained for ten days to

2
00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:13.220
report warming of the forepaw.

3
00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:15.100
They completely failed.

4
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.040
That sounds backwards.

5
00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:19.840
A cold receptor should matter for cold.

6
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.040
So why would a mouse without it miss warmth?

7
00:00:23.983 --> 00:00:30.023
Here is the task. A head-fixed mouse is trained to report a temperature step on its

8
00:00:30.023 --> 00:00:37.503
forepaw. A Peltier surface, 8 by 8 mm, holds 32 °C, then

9
00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:42.183
steps. Trained mice reported a warming step of 1 °C.

10
00:00:42.883 --> 00:00:44.683
The mouse licks to report it.

11
00:00:45.417 --> 00:00:51.817
Alongside the behaviour, the group recorded single fibres from forepaw skin, kept

12
00:00:51.817 --> 00:00:54.757
alive outside the animal with its nerve attached.

13
00:00:55.677 --> 00:00:57.577
This is a skin-nerve preparation.

14
00:00:58.537 --> 00:01:00.177
Each tick is one spike.

15
00:01:01.217 --> 00:01:04.057
They warmed the skin at one degree per second.

16
00:01:04.957 --> 00:01:10.737
One population, the polymodal C fibres, increased its firing as the skin warmed.

17
00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:12.697
Warming excites them.

18
00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:16.840
A second population answered the opposite way.

19
00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:22.940
These are cool-sensitive C fibres, about 19% of the thermosensitive fibres

20
00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:30.820
recorded. In a bath at 27 °C, they fired all the time, between 0.2 and 6 Hz.

21
00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:34.060
Warming reduced that ongoing rate.

22
00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:41.400
The group used 27 °C because thermal imaging showed awake forepaw skin at 26 to

23
00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:47.340
28 °C. At the usual 32 °C bath, this population had not been seen.

24
00:01:48.233 --> 00:01:51.913
Temperature is not read off one channel at a time.

25
00:01:52.833 --> 00:01:55.053
Warmth has two signals at once.

26
00:01:55.593 --> 00:01:57.133
Some fibres speed up.

27
00:01:57.933 --> 00:01:59.393
Cool fibres slow down.

28
00:02:00.293 --> 00:02:06.513
Without TRPM8, the cool fibres lose their ongoing firing, and half of the warmth

29
00:02:06.513 --> 00:02:11.173
signal is gone. Write that as reduced cool input.

30
00:02:12.173 --> 00:02:16.413
No central circuit that flips the sign of the cool signal has been identified.

31
00:02:17.267 --> 00:02:18.867
Remember the bath.

32
00:02:19.767 --> 00:02:24.547
A signal that looks absent at one baseline may be there at another.

33
00:02:25.647 --> 00:02:30.307
The resting condition is part of the stimulus, not a neutral background.

34
00:02:31.547 --> 00:02:36.687
In the mouse forepaw, warmth is read from excitation and from silence.
